[EXPLAIN] Architecture selection frequency
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  For each description, how often each algorithm combination won the inner selection across folds.
  If one                 combination wins most folds, it is a stable choice; if many different
  ones win, the data cannot clearly                 distinguish them (many are about equally
  good). Step 03 uses the most frequent winner. SVM appearing very often                 suggests
  smooth, similarity-based models fit this dataset well.
